Subject: [PATCH] core: expose the composited frame's SHA-256 for determinism tests

T026 shipped a change to the render path and its device-side output equality was
never verified. The before/after PNG comparison was worthless because the two
captures were of different game states -- one was frame 434, the other some
unknown earlier moment. What existed was an exhaustive host-side proof over all
32768 pixel values, which cannot catch a stride error, a rotation mistake, or a
wrong buffer.

That gap is why "the output is unchanged" is currently an argument. This exposes
the digest the core already computes so it can be a check.

render_lines_impl() already hashes the composited BGR555 frame per frame, but
only behind sc_core_logging_enabled(), which T028 measured at 14.5% of the
frame and which the 3DS port therefore leaves off by default. The accessor makes
that existing work reachable without changing when it happens, so nothing about
the default build path moves.

The header documents the two traps, because both would produce a confident wrong
answer rather than an obvious failure:

  - With logging off the digest is NOT recomputed; it holds the previous frame's
    value. A caller that forgets to enable logging compares stale data and
    concludes the frames match when they were never hashed.
  - It covers the composited frame only. It cannot see the frontend's rotation,
    channel order or stride, which is precisely where T026's change lived.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
--- a/include/simcity_static_recomp.h
+++ b/include/simcity_static_recomp.h
@@ -168,6 +168,29 @@
 
    Read-only, like frame_bgra. Valid until the next advance. */
 const uint16_t *simcity_recomp_frame_bgr555(const SimCityRecomp *instance);
+
+/* SHA-256 of the composited BGR555 frame, as 64 lowercase hex chars + NUL.
+ *
+ * The digest render_lines_impl already computes for its own report -- but only
+ * while sc_core_logging_enabled() is true, which T028 measured at 14.5% of the
+ * frame. Exposed here so a harness can assert two runs produced identical
+ * output, which is the only way to make "this change did not alter the
+ * picture" a check rather than an opinion.
+ *
+ * Two things a caller must know:
+ *
+ *   - It is all '0' until a frame has been rendered, and it HOLDS ITS PREVIOUS
+ *     VALUE if logging is off, because nothing recomputes it. A caller that
+ *     compares digests without enabling logging first is comparing stale data
+ *     and will conclude the frames match when they were never hashed. The 3DS
+ *     port leaves the core log off by default for performance, so a determinism
+ *     run must turn it on.
+ *   - It covers the composited frame only. It says nothing about the frontend's
+ *     rotation, channel order or stride -- exactly where T026's change could
+ *     have broken the output without this digest noticing.
+ *
+ * Read-only. Valid until the next rendered frame. */
+const char *simcity_recomp_frame_bgr555_sha256(const SimCityRecomp *instance);
 uint32_t simcity_recomp_frame_width(const SimCityRecomp *instance);
 int simcity_recomp_widescreen_enabled(const SimCityRecomp *instance);
 int simcity_recomp_set_widescreen(SimCityRecomp *instance, int enabled,
--- a/src/simcity_static_recomp.c
+++ b/src/simcity_static_recomp.c
@@ -1112,6 +1112,10 @@
     return instance ? instance->bgr555 : NULL;
 }
 
+const char *simcity_recomp_frame_bgr555_sha256(const SimCityRecomp *instance) {
+    return instance ? instance->video.bgr555_sha256 : NULL;
+}
+
 uint32_t simcity_recomp_frame_width(const SimCityRecomp *instance) {
     return instance && instance->widescreen ?
         SIMCITY_RECOMP_WIDESCREEN_WIDTH : SIMCITY_RECOMP_FRAME_WIDTH;
